e_patch_sha256":"ab0c5a3bcef56a659f9cdbefe5426f7d904b28754f2190ab89bdaa551a9aa326","finding_commits":{"review:5632215369":"76403594ab72932f30d6be28ea73643d21044d5f"},"parent":"42ed545ad49e478e856556edde3f7b4f63d54e73","patch_sha256":"ab0c5a3bcef56a659f9cdbefe5426f7d904b28754f2190ab89bdaa551a9aa326","tree":"49925dded33c58cbbb85f3f2370d50798c0ef79f"},"dispositions":{"findings":[{"analysis":"Confirmed on the frozen implementation: after a nested pipeline sync returns normally, Response.get() escapes with the same Redis exception but the outer pipeline reports redis.clients.jedis.exceptions.JedisDataException rather than WRONGTYPE. Detachment now retains every captured error identity in the enclosing context without assigning its firstServerErrorThrowable. The new agent-backed deferred-response regression and helper coverage pass; handled nested errors still leave the parent successful.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"review:5632215369"}],"input_identity":{},"outcome":"fixes","request_digest":"1b444917c87d5d4c76c01106a438662c83babac68ee12e20fa068c4359d959b3","schema":2},"download_sha256":"cbb0a46eabe006b0d31cfd0726c642c654fb718c392951af1ee12da8dd9d543e","frozen_sha":"42ed545ad49e478e856556edde3f7b4f63d54e73","pr":20792,"publication_eligible":false,"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","request_digest":"1b444917c87d5d4c76c01106a438662c83babac68ee12e20fa068c4359d959b3","request_id":"51704cce1d2448589acb428b9baabfd7","run_attempt":1,"run_id":40015073907,"schema":2,"scope":"Structural/Git verification only. No target code or tests are executed.","server_artifact_digest":"sha256:cbb0a46eabe006b0d31cfd0726c642c654fb718c392951af1ee12da8dd9d543e","verification":"verified","verification_run":{"attempt":1,"id":40018692067},"workflow_revision":"98fb6cdde0b957dd9fac1921637140b3abe6e57b"},"request":{"authorized_actor_id":218610,"baseline_review_ids":[5595037791,5602613364,5602768035,5603335990,5604242345,5604382473,5604602327,5605888987,5607831660,5607902480,5608431909,5608480756,5608527521,5608588503,5608695989,5608828028,5608935961,5609221046,5609269429,5609280086,5609364335,5609495079,5609541436,5609695781,5609823325,5609858511,5609923088,5610093202,5610172868,5610401756,5610513991,5610515462,5610554759,5610589942,5610713463,5610917078,5610973195,5611400932,5611523788,5611595016,5611671404,5611833027,5611956600,5612109515,5612187484,5612284156,5612357573,5612866704,5620026160,5620359674,5620451249,5620654372,5620814939,5623027445,5623140277,5623239329,5623283967,5623331172,5623405546,5623464530,5623486701,5623638759,5624190425,5631134927,5631242964,5632215369],"budgets":{"max_iterations":5,"propagation_seconds":120,"retention_days":14,"worker_timeout_minutes":30},"commit_author":{"id":218610,"login":"trask"},"findings":[{"body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### \ud83d\udd35 Needs a closer look\n\nDeferred nested-pipeline failures can lose server-error confirmation and receive incorrect error classifications on spans and duration metrics.\n\n**No open issues** \ud83c\udf89\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>1 previously missed issue</strong></summary>\n\nIn code that hasn't changed since last review\n\n<details>\n<summary><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> Preserve deferred nested Redis error identity during detachment</summary>\n\n`instrumentation/\u200bjedis/\u200bjedis-common/\u200bjavaagent/\u200bsrc/\u200bmain/\u200bjava/\u200bio/\u200bopentelemetry/\u200bjavaagent/\u200binstrumentation/\u200bjedis/\u200bcommon/\u200bJedisRequestContext.java:115`\n\n[Javaagent] A nested pipeline's deferred response loses its server-error confirmation here. In a Jedis 4.0.0 response `Builder`, save the `Response` from `nested.get(\"wrong-type\")` on another client, call `nested.sync()`, then call `response.get()`. The sync captures `WRONGTYPE` but returns normally, so this guard transfers no confirmation. The subsequent `get()` throws that same exception, which the outer `syncAndReturnAll()` returns as a failed result. The outer span and duration metric therefore use the exception class instead of `WRONGTYPE`.\n\nPreserve captured error identities when detaching, including normal nested-batch completion, without setting the enclosing context's `firstServerErrorThrowable`. This keeps handled errors from failing the parent while allowing deferred failures to be classified correctly. Add a regression for this deferred-response path alongside the nested-command tests.\n</details>\n</details>\n\n<sub>Review effort: Balanced</sub>","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5632215369","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5632215369}],"frozen_at":1792785225,"frozen_at_iso":"2026-10-23T19:53:45Z","frozen_sha":"42ed545ad49e478e856556edde3f7b4f63d54e73","head_ref":"copilot/trask-jedis-redis-server-errors","head_repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","head_repo_id":210933087,"input_mode":"direct","launch_run":{"actor_id":218610,"attempt":1,"id":40014966771},"loop_kind":"copilot_review","metadata":{"body":"<!--\nCHANGELOG.md is generated from merged pull requests. Do not add an entry unless this PR introduces\na deprecation or breaking change.\n-->\n\nClassify Redis server errors for Jedis 2, 3, and 4+ on spans and database duration metrics. A confirmed `WRONGTYPE details` reply produces `error.type=\"WRONGTYPE\"`.\n\nPreserve usable ASCII prefixes verbatim. Dedicated server exceptions, non-ASCII or missing prefixes, and client failures retain exception-class fallback. Successful operations omit `error.type`.\n\nPropagate actual failures through command, pipeline, and transaction completion, including error results returned inside batches.","title":"Classify Jedis Redis server errors"},"mode":"publish","pr":20792,"pr_author_id":198982749,"protocol":"git-candidate-v1","publication":{"auth_mode":"fine_grained_pat","authorized_actor_id":218610,"authorized_at":1792785228,"generation":7,"max_pipelines":5,"phase":"90118556925a432f9754b1f8c2afb4f0","profile":"git-candidate-v1","required_checks":[]},"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","repo_id":210933087,"request_id":"51704cce1d2448589acb428b9baabfd7","schema":2,"source_private":false,"target_private":false,"workflow_ref":"review-loop-revisions/98fb6cdde0b957dd9fac1921637140b3abe6e57b","workflow_revision":"98fb6cdde0b957dd9fac1921637140b3abe6e57b"},"review_request":{"baseline_review_ids":[5595037791,5602613364,5602768035,5603335990,5604242345,5604382473,5604602327,5605888987,5607831660,5607902480,5608431909,5608480756,5608527521,5608588503,5608695989,5608828028,5608935961,5609221046,5609269429,5609280086,5609364335,5609495079,5609541436,5609695781,5609823325,5609858511,5609923088,5610093202,5610172868,5610401756,5610513991,5610515462,5610554759,5610589942,5610713463,5610917078,5610973195,5611400932,5611523788,5611595016,5611671404,5611833027,5611956600,5612109515,5612187484,5612284156,5612357573,5612866704,5620026160,5620359674,5620451249,5620654372,5620814939,5623027445,5623140277,5623239329,5623283967,5623331172,5623405546,5623464530,5623486701,5623638759,5624190425,5631134927,5631242964,5632215369],"baseline_run_ids":[40018912961,40018912967,40018913324,40018913650,40018913790],"claim":"aa206eaef7684a0ca0a6149ae41f2856","confirmation":{"kind":"submitted_review","review_ids":[5634095248]},"owner":{"attempt":"1","run_id":"40018692067"},"recorded_at":1792787069,"sha":"76403594ab72932f30d6be28ea73643d21044d5f","status":"confirmed"},"run":{"attempt":1,"conclusion":"success","id":40015073907,"url":"https://github.com/trask/copilo